    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A beautifully restored thatched farmhouse of exceptional character\n\nApproached through a gravelled courtyard and set beneath a traditional thatched roof, The Cottage immediately conveys a sense of history and authenticity. The whitewashed façade and a distinctive painted entrance door, provides an inviting introduction to this beautifully preserved farmhouse.\n\nBeyond the entrance hall, the interior unfolds as a collection of characterful and deeply comfortable living spaces, where exposed timber beams, lime-rendered walls and original stone floors reflect the heritage of the property. At the heart of the home lies the farmhouse kitchen, centred around a traditional range and open-hearth fireplace, creating a natural gathering space. Bespoke cabinetry and original detailing reinforce the enduring appeal of this room, while an adjoining utility room provides practical ancillary accommodation.\n\nAt the heart of the house is a welcoming reception room, centred around a traditional open-hearth fireplace and enhanced by exposed beams, original joinery and a wealth of period character. A separate study provides a practical and flexible space, well suited to modern living while remaining entirely in keeping with the historic nature of the property.\n\nA bathroom completes the ground floor accommodation, thoughtfully presented in keeping with the age and character of the house.\n\nA staircase rises to the first floor, where the accommodation continues beneath the sweep of the thatched roof. The master bedroom benefits from en suite facilities and enjoys views over garden. Two further bedrooms, each characterised by exposed roof timbers, original detailing and a peaceful outlook, complete the upper floor.\n\nOutside, the traditional farmhouse setting is further enhanced by an impressive range of stone outbuildings arranged around the courtyard. These attractive buildings contribute significantly to the property's appeal and offer potential for sympathetic restoration, subject to the necessary planning permissions. Given the property's proximity to the Boyne Valley and its wealth of internationally recognised heritage attractions, the outbuildings may also present opportunities for tourism-related accommodation or ancillary uses, subject to the requisite consents. To the rear, a mature woodland garden provides a private setting, beyond which an adjoining paddock extends the grounds."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Beautifully restored 400-year-old thatched farmhouse</li><li>Winner of Period Living Magazine's \"Best Restoration Britain & Ireland\" Award 2011</li><li>Traditional stone outbuildings</li><li>Residence retaining exceptional original period features throughout</li><li>Mature woodland garden with adjoining paddock </li><li>Conveniently located close to M1, N2 and Dublin Airport</li></ul>"
      },
